  %% 1. The Console sends everything a person does to the API as a request.
  console -->|1| api
  %% 2. The Console asks Sign-in who the person is, and Sign-in issues the session that every request carries.
  console -->|2| sign_in
  %% 3. The API asks the policy engine whether each request is allowed, and the engine answers with a reason.
  api -->|3| policy
  %% 4. The step gateway passes a custom step's requests to the API. It forwards only the step routes and answers 404 to everything else.
  gateway -->|4| api
  %% 5. The API records every decision, and the history behind it, in the database.
  api -->|5| database
  %% 6. The API creates a key in object storage for one task at a time, so a task can open only the files it was allowed.
  api -->|6| storage
  %% 7. The API starts a long job, such as a pipeline run, in the workflow engine.
  api -->|7| workflow
  %% 8. The workflow engine hands the job to the worker and keeps it going if the worker stops, so the job can resume.
  workflow -->|8| worker
  %% 9. The workflow engine hands the writing of a large table to the table worker.
  workflow -->|9| table_worker
  %% 10. The worker starts a sandboxed agent run on a network with no route to the internet.
  worker -->|10| agent
  %% 11. The worker starts the derivation runner, which runs one query with no network connection.
  worker -->|11| derivation
  %% 12. The worker starts a custom pipeline step, which is an organisation's own code, on a network of its own.
  worker -->|12| custom
  %% 13. The custom step reaches the platform only through the step gateway.
  custom -->|13| gateway
